<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="18.2" level="1">Crimes and Offenses Generally</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="9" level="2">Crimes Against Peace and Order</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="1" level="3">Riot and Unlawful Assembly</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>18.2-408</section_number>
	<catch_line>Conspiracy; incitement, etc., to riot</catch_line>
	<text>
		Any person who conspires with others to cause or produce a riot, or directs, incites, or solicits other persons who participate in a riot to acts of force or violence, shall be guilty of a Class 5 felony.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 18.1-254.5:1; 1971, Ex. Sess., c. 251; 1975, cc. 14, 15.</history>
</law>
